<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8018" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cīmon</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cīmo</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 5, 4</span></i>, ext. 2),
			ōnis, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίμων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Father of Miltiades</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Milt.
			1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A son of Miltiades</i>, <i>a
				distinguished general of the Athenians</i>, <i>whose life is written by Nepos</i>, <i><span class="en">Nep. Cim.
			1</span></i> sqq.; cf. also <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 2, 18, 64</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen. Contr. 4, 24, p. 275</span></i> sqq. Bip.;
				<i><span class="en">Val.
				Max. 5, 3</span></i>, ext. 3; <i><span class="en">Just. 2,
				15, 18</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
